---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SafeToAdd from '../components/SafeToAdd.astro';

const gentifiUrl = 'https://mcp.gentifi.com/mcp';

const tools = [
  { name: 'find_businesses', does: 'Finds shops on Gentifi by name, place, kind of shop or what they sell.' },
  { name: 'get_business_info', does: 'A shop’s opening hours, contact details and how ordering works.' },
  { name: 'search_catalogue', does: 'What a shop sells, with prices, stock and when they were last updated.' },
  { name: 'check_availability', does: 'Whether a shop has enough of one item, and when it’s available.' },
  { name: 'prepare_order', does: 'Works out a reservation or order and its total, with a link to a confirmation page. Nothing is ordered or sent until you check it there and tap Confirm.' },
];

const asks = [
  'Does Hollow Lane Farm Shop have free-range eggs?',
  'When is Hollow Lane Farm Shop open?',
  'Which shops on Gentifi sell sourdough?',
  'Reserve a dozen eggs at Hollow Lane Farm Shop for Saturday.',
];
---
<Base
  title="Add local shops to Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini and Grok · Gentifi"
  description="Add Gentifi to Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini or Grok, then ask local shops what they have, prices and opening times, and prepare reservations you confirm yourself."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Gentifi connector</span>
        <h1>Connect local shops to your AI assistant.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Add Gentifi to your AI assistant or agent, then ask local shops what they have, prices, stock and opening
          times. Your AI can prepare a reservation or order; you check it on a Gentifi confirmation page, tap Confirm, then send it to the shop or finish on its own checkout.
        </p>
        <SafeToAdd />
        <p class="link">The link: <code>{gentifiUrl}</code></p>

        <h2>Add it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Claude:</strong> Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector. Name it Gentifi, paste the link, then confirm.</li>
          <li><strong>ChatGPT:</strong> in a browser, not the app: <a href="https://chatgpt.com/plugins">chatgpt.com/plugins</a> → Add (top right) → Add custom MCP server. Name it Gentifi, paste the link and choose no authentication. Then type @ in a chat to pick it.</li>
          <li><strong>Gemini:</strong> on a computer: <a href="https://gemini.google.com/app">gemini.google.com/app</a> → Settings → Connected Apps → Custom apps → add. Paste the link, click Next and follow the steps. Then type @ in a chat to pick it. It works in the Gemini phone app once added.</li>
          <li><strong>Grok:</strong> <a href="https://grok.com/connectors">grok.com/connectors</a> → New Connector → Custom. Name it Gentifi, paste the link and choose no authentication. Then ask about any shop in a chat.</li>
          <li><strong>Hermes Agent:</strong> run <code>hermes mcp add gentifi --url {gentifiUrl}</code>, then <code>/reload-mcp</code> in a chat.</li>
          <li><strong>Other AI apps:</strong> paste the link wherever the app lets you add connectors (sometimes called MCP servers).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Try asking</h2>
        <ul>{asks.map((a) => <li>“{a}”</li>)}</ul>
        <p>
          Hollow Lane Farm Shop is a fictional shop for trying Gentifi out, so nothing you reserve there is real. Real
          shops are joining, starting in Bristol and South Gloucestershire.
        </p>

        <h2>What it can do</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{tools.map((t) => <tr><td><code>{t.name}</code></td><td>{t.does}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Every tool only reads. Your AI asks shops by name, or by the id <code>find_businesses</code> returns.</p>

        <h2>What it won’t do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It never places an order, sends a message or takes a payment. You confirm every order on a Gentifi confirmation page, which gives you a reference, then send it to the shop by email or finish on the shop’s own checkout.</li>
          <li>It can’t change a shop’s information. Shops keep their own catalogue up to date.</li>
          <li>It doesn’t ask for your name, contact details, location or chat history.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
        <p>
          From each shop’s own catalogue, usually a spreadsheet the shop updates. Gentifi re-reads online sheets every ten
          minutes, and your AI is told when prices and stock were last updated, so it can say so.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          We don’t keep what you ask. See <a href="/privacy#connector">how the connector handles your requests</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="support">Support</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:gentifiai@gmail.com">gentifiai@gmail.com</a> with any problem or question about the
          connector. For an order you’ve sent, contact the shop directly.
        </p>
        <p>
          Developers: the connector is built with the open-source <a href="/toolkit">Gentifi toolkit</a>. It is the one
          connector for every shop on Gentifi: shops don’t have connectors of their own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: calc(46rem + var(--gutter) * 2); display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .prose h1 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 18px; }
  .prose p, .prose li { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .prose li strong { color: var(--teal); }
  .prose ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .prose a { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; }
  .prose code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .link code { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grey); vertical-align: top; }
  th { color: var(--teal); }
  td { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  td code { color: var(--teal); white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
